    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR aims to make generated extension documentation stable for “released but non-ratified” extensions by introducing a `release_date` field and using it to populate AsciiDoc `:revdate:` instead of defaulting to `Date.today`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add `release_date` to `Udb::ExtensionVersion` and the extension JSON schema, and require it for `state: nonstandard-released`.\n- Update ext-doc generation helpers to prefer `release_date` for `:revdate:` when the version is `nonstandard-released`.\n- Update Xqci 0.13.0 metadata to `state: nonstandard-released` with a concrete `release_date`, and add corresponding state text in AsciiDoc helpers.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 5 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/obj/extension.rb | Adds `release_date` accessor on extension versions. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/lib/udb-gen/generators/ext_doc/helpers.rb | Uses `release_date` to compute `revdate` for `nonstandard-released`. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/lib/udb-gen/adoc_helpers.rb | Adds messaging for `nonstandard-released` state in generated AsciiDoc. |\r\n| spec/schemas/ext_schema.json | Requires and defines `release_date` for `nonstandard-released` extension versions. |\r\n| spec/custom/isa/qc_iu/ext/Xqci.yaml | Marks Xqci 0.13.0 as `nonstandard-released` and sets `release_date`. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
